    <!--
      Two cereal boxes placed to occlude the Pringles can, 0.06 x 0.16 x 0.24 m
      and as tall as it. They were first put either side of the can at +/-0.13 m,
      which was wrong twice over: the fusion cube is 0.3 m centred on the target,
      so 5 of each box's 6 cm sat *inside* the volume being fused, and 0.062 m
      was room for the gripper's opening but not for the hand and wrist to reach
      in, so every IK solution came back in collision.

      The table top is 0.68 x 1.13 m at (1.56, 2.58) turned 90 degrees, so it
      runs x 0.995-2.125, y 2.24-2.92. The can at x 1.1 is 10 cm from the left
      edge, and a symmetric pair clear of the cube would put the left box on the
      floor. So they go where the table has room: one to the right, one behind.
      Both clear the cube (x 0.95-1.25, y 2.17-2.47) and leave the front-left
      quadrant open, which is the approach the policy now has to find.

      The scene graph is deliberately untouched: it still places the can where
      the can still is, so the mission navigates there as before and only the
      view is obstructed, which is the point. These two boxes are unmapped
      clutter, as far as everything upstream of the camera is concerned.
    -->
    <include>
      <static>false</static>
      <name>demo_occluder_behind</name>
      <pose>1.10 2.56 0.522 0 0 0</pose>
      <uri>model://cereal_box</uri>
    </include>
    <include>
      <static>false</static>
      <name>demo_occluder_right</name>
      <pose>1.32 2.34 0.522 0 0 0</pose>
      <uri>model://cereal_box</uri>
    </include>
